./COMPATIBILITY.md:242:| config | partial | vault-backed local/global config is supported; section operations `--remove-section <name>` and `--rename-section <old> <new>` (transactional; use Git's section/subsection identity, so `--remove-section branch` deletes `branch.<key>` but not the `branch.feature.*` subsection; rename preserves each value's encryption flag and refuses an existing destination section; missing section exits 128, identical rename exits 2) are supported; `-z`/`--null` NUL-delimited output (`value\0` for get/get-all, `key\nvalue\0` for `--get-regexp`/`--list`, `key\0` with `--name-only`, `origin\0` prefix with `--show-origin`; rejected with the Libra-only `--ssh-keys`/`--gpg-keys`/`--vault` views) is supported; type canonicalization `--type=<bool|int|path>` and the `--bool`/`--int`/`--path` shortcuts (bool variants → true/false, int k/m/g 1024-based multipliers, path `~`/`~/` expansion) applies both when reading (get modes) and when setting (the value is validated/canonicalized before storage, matching `git config --type`: `yes` → `true`, `1k` → `1024`; an invalid value errors without storing); a non-get/non-set mode is rejected (exit 129) is supported; the `--system` scope (`/etc/libra/config.db`, overridable via `LIBRA_CONFIG_SYSTEM_DB`; lowest cascade precedence; vault-encrypted secrets rejected in this scope) is supported; the `upgrade.*` namespace is intentionally-different (reserved, Libra-only: stored in `{LIBRA_HOME}/upgrade/settings.json`, only single-value `set`/`get`/`unset` with `--global` are accepted, `unset` resets `upgrade.mode` to `off` keeping the file, other scopes/multivalue/type/section/conflicting-action spellings and `--get-regexp` patterns matching `upgrade.mode` fail closed as usage errors (`LBR-CLI-002`; a corrupt or unreadable settings file is `LBR-UPGRADE-001`), and stale SQLite `upgrade.*` rows are suppressed from `list` and non-matching `--get-regexp`); editor round-trip and includeIf are incomplete; the per-worktree config overlay exists and is written only by `worktree add`/migrate probe — the public `config --worktree` write surface is deferred (plan-20260714 DEFER-09), and overlay values tighten but never loosen the repository scope; bare `libra config <key>` reads the stored value like `git config <key>` (last value wins for a multi-valued key; unset exits 1 with `LBR-CLI-002`; an encrypted value renders `<REDACTED>` exactly as `config get` does), except that **intentionally-different: bare read of a protected key keeps the interactive assignment path** — for keys `is_sensitive_key` classifies as protected, `libra config <key>` still prompts for a new value instead of readingand reports the protected-key error with exit 2 when no terminal is available; the global scope stores its SQLite database at `<XDG_CONFIG_HOME or ~/.config>/libra/config.db` (defaulting to `<home>/.config/libra/config.db` on every platform, macOS included) and keeps the legacy `<home>/.libra/config.db` as the active file while it is the only store present, so reads and writes never split across two databases; `config path --json` and `doctor --global-schema` report `path_source` as `LIBRA_CONFIG_GLOBAL_DB`, `xdg`, `home` or `legacy`, plus `legacy_path`/`legacy_exists`/`migration_pending` (additive; `report_version` stays 1) `core.filemode` is read case-insensitively (Unix default `true`): with `false`, staging keeps an existing entry's mode and records new paths as `100644`, while `--chmod`/`--cacheinfo` stay explicit; an invalid value fails `add`/`status` closed before any write; with `core.filemode=true` (Unix default) a mode-only worktree change (owner-execute bit differs, content unchanged) is reported by `status`, rendered by `diff`, staged by `add`/`commit -a`/`update-index <path>`, and stashed by `stash push`, while `false` ignores mode-only differences and entry-type changes (regular file ↔ symlink) stay visible (plan issues/470 FM-03, FM-04). |
